      "narrative": "Mara Venn's fingers pause mid-air, the tips stained with ink and something darker near the cuticles. She's been rolling a copper coin between them, and now it clatters onto the scarred tabletop.\n\n\"I'd have to think on that,\" she says, her voice a low rasp that doesn't quite reach the next table. Her eyes drift past you, toward the shuttered window where grey morning light fights through the slats. \"The lock work on that gate... it's been years since anyone touched it proper.\"\n\nShe's lying. Or she's forgetting. Something flickers behind those sharp eyes \u2014 recognition, maybe, or calculation \u2014 but she shakes her head slowly.\n\n\"Can't say I ever knew who held that contract. Gate's been sealed longer than most folks care to remember.\""
    },
