      "narrative": "Your voice rings out across the still water, echoing off the cracked stone \u2014 \"Bram! Old Bram!\" \u2014 and then fades into the damp air.\n\nNothing answers.\n\nThe black iron of the gate holds its silence. The water laps against the dock stones with a wet, rhythmic sound. Somewhere on the far side of the channel, a bird calls once and stops.\n\nNo footsteps. No creak of a door. No voice.\n\nSix days dead, Mara said. The silence here feels final \u2014 the kind that settles into places where no one comes anymore. The frayed rope hanging from the cleat shifts slightly in a breeze you can't feel, trailing its end in the dark water.\n\nThe fused lock hangs motionless on its hasp. The gate waits."
