      "narrative": "You drop to a crouch beneath the arch, your fingers brushing the grit and dust that carpets the stone landing. You scan the ground methodically \u2014 every crack, every shadow, every scrap of debris \u2014 searching for a dropped clue, a scuff mark, anything that might tell you what happened here.\n\nNothing.\n\nThe dust lies smooth and undisturbed, settled in a uniform grey layer across every stone. No footprints. No drag marks. No sign that anyone has passed this way in days. The silt at the water's edge is unbroken save for the natural lapping of the current.\n\nYour eyes trace the base of the gate, the moss-crusted hinges, the rust-flakes scattered like dried blood on the stone. But there's nothing hidden here. Nothing out of place. The ground beneath the arch holds its secrets well \u2014 or perhaps there never were any secrets to find.\n\nThe fused lock hangs silently above you. The frayed rope trails in the water. The Ash Gate offers nothing but stillness."
